      {
        "id": "personal-api-key",
        "label": "Personal API key",
        "description": "Paste a Personal API key from your PostHog account. Stored locally \u2014 never sent anywhere except PostHog itself.",
        "recommended": false,
        "how_to": "## Generate a PostHog Personal API key\n\nPersonal API keys give Anton your account-level scopes \u2014 they can read across every project you have access to (you can also scope them down). Project IDs and host vary by where your PostHog instance lives.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. Sign in to PostHog at [us.posthog.com](https://us.posthog.com), [eu.posthog.com](https://eu.posthog.com), or your self-hosted URL.\n2. Click your profile icon (top right) \u2192 **Account settings**.\n3. Open the **Personal API keys** tab.\n4. Click **+ Create personal API key**. Name it `Anton`, optionally restrict the scopes to read-only or specific projects.\n5. Copy the generated key (starts with `phx_\u2026`). Paste it into **Personal API key** below.\n6. Pick the **Host** that matches where you signed in (US Cloud, EU Cloud, or paste your self-hosted URL).\n7. On submit, Cowork lists the PostHog projects accessible to this key so you can choose by name. You can also enter a numeric Project ID manually when needed.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The Personal API key is a credential \u2014 anyone with it can read everything you can read in PostHog. Anton stores it locally; rotate it from the same Account settings panel if you suspect exposure.\n- Project-scoped Project API keys (the `phc_\u2026` ones used by SDK ingestion) are NOT what you want here \u2014 those can only WRITE events, not read them.\n- Read [PostHog's API authentication docs](https://posthog.com/docs/api#how-to-obtain-a-personal-api-key).\n",
        "help_url": "https://posthog.com/docs/api#how-to-obtain-a-personal-api-key",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "personal_api_key",
            "label": "Personal API key",
            "type": "password",
            "required": true,
            "secret": true,
            "placeholder": "phx_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
            "description": "Starts with phx_ \u2014 generate from PostHog \u2192 Account settings \u2192 Personal API keys."
          },
          {
            "name": "host",
            "label": "Host",
            "type": "select",
            "required": true,
            "default": "https://us.posthog.com",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "https://us.posthog.com",
                "label": "US Cloud (us.posthog.com)"
              },
              {
                "value": "https://eu.posthog.com",
                "label": "EU Cloud (eu.posthog.com)"
              },
              {
                "value": "custom",
                "label": "Self-hosted (enter URL)"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Match the region you signed in to."
          },
          {
            "name": "custom_host",
            "label": "Self-hosted URL",
            "type": "url",
            "required": false,
            "placeholder": "https://posthog.your-company.com",
            "description": "Only fill in if you picked Self-hosted above."
          },
          {
            "name": "project_id",
            "label": "Project ID",
            "type": "text",
            "required": true,
            "placeholder": "12345",
            "description": "Leave blank to choose an accessible project by name after submitting, or enter the numeric ID from your PostHog URL."
          }
        ]
      }
